2. 1976 - Civil War Start: LEx Lebanon crashes 66.5 -> 36.5y
3. 1982 - Israeli Invasion: Second crash 60 -> 47y
4. 1990-2019 Post-war: Fast recovery to 78y
5. 2020-2021: Lebanon drops 78.1 -> 73.5y, World 72.4 -> 71y
6. 2022-2023: Rebound to 77.9y

### 4.6 Migration Analysis

Here Chart 9 - Chart9_Immigration1950_2100
[Line plot NetMigrations 1950-2100]

2019 economic crisis starts: Banks freeze dollars, Lira devalues 90%, People WANT to leave but CAN'T afford ticket + visa. Outflow drops from -270 to -150.
2020-2021 COVID travel bans: Airports closed. Both in and out = 0. Net rate goes from -250 to -30 automatically because Immigrants = 0 and Emigrants = 0, so Net = 0.
2022+ UN projection smooths to 0: UN WPP 2024 assumes migration returns to normal long-term average -0.9 per 1000.

